WEBVTT

00:03.840 --> 00:04.120
Okay.

00:04.120 --> 00:06.840
So now we're going to start with the first function the date add.

00:06.840 --> 00:14.760
So what is date add date add can allow us to add or subtract a specific time interval to or from a date.

00:14.760 --> 00:16.880
So let's understand how the date add works.

00:16.880 --> 00:20.400
So here again we have our date August 20th, 2025.

00:20.400 --> 00:24.160
So now in some scenarios we would like to add years to our dates.

00:24.160 --> 00:27.360
So for example let's say I would like to add three years to our date.

00:27.360 --> 00:29.360
So we can do that using the date add.

00:29.360 --> 00:33.800
So if you do that in the output you will get 2028 August 20th.

00:33.840 --> 00:38.120
Only the date part is changed and where we have added three years.

00:38.120 --> 00:40.800
But in other scenarios you would like to go and add months.

00:40.800 --> 00:44.120
So for example, let's go and add two months to the August.

00:44.120 --> 00:47.680
So in the output you will get 20, 2510, 20.

00:47.720 --> 00:49.520
With that we have added two months.

00:49.520 --> 00:52.800
And of course we can go and add days to our dates.

00:52.800 --> 00:56.040
So for example we're going to go and add five days to our dates.

00:56.040 --> 01:01.840
So in the output we'll get the same year 2025, the same month August, but only the day will be changed

01:01.840 --> 01:03.200
to 25.

01:03.200 --> 01:06.120
So we have added five days to the original dates.

01:06.120 --> 01:10.640
And of course we can go and subtract dates even though that the function called date add.

01:10.640 --> 01:15.390
So for example we can go and subtract three years from our dates and we will get.

01:15.390 --> 01:18.950
So if you do that you will get 2022 August 20th.

01:18.990 --> 01:24.230
Or if you go and subtract two months from our dates so it can stay the same year 2025.

01:24.270 --> 01:28.390
But this time instead of August, we will go back to June with the same date 20.

01:28.430 --> 01:32.270
And the same thing can happen for the days if you go and subtract five days.

01:32.270 --> 01:37.550
So the same year, 2025, the same month August, but only the day is going to be instead of 20, it's

01:37.550 --> 01:38.510
going to be 15.

01:38.510 --> 01:45.110
So as you can see with the date add, you can manipulate the years, the month, and the days by subtracting

01:45.110 --> 01:47.110
or adding new intervals.

01:47.110 --> 01:49.110
So this is how the date add works.

01:49.110 --> 01:49.430
All right.

01:49.430 --> 01:51.350
So now let's check the syntax of the date add.

01:51.350 --> 01:53.390
And here things a little bit more complicated.

01:53.390 --> 01:55.830
We have to provide three informations.

01:55.830 --> 01:57.230
The first one is apart.

01:57.270 --> 01:58.110
What do you want to add.

01:58.150 --> 02:01.790
Do you want to add years or months or days and so on.

02:02.030 --> 02:04.150
Then the second one is interval.

02:04.150 --> 02:07.350
So it's like how many days, how many years how many months.

02:07.390 --> 02:09.270
And then the last one is the dates.

02:09.270 --> 02:14.510
This is the date that we're going to be manipulating by adding or subtracting intervals.

02:14.550 --> 02:15.830
Let's check the following example.

02:15.830 --> 02:17.870
We are saying here date add.

02:17.870 --> 02:18.830
So what is the part?

02:18.830 --> 02:19.990
Here is a year.

02:20.030 --> 02:24.660
That means we want to manipulate only the ear parts, then the interval here is two.

02:24.700 --> 02:25.580
So it is positive.

02:25.580 --> 02:27.980
We want to add two years.

02:27.980 --> 02:32.180
So it's going to go to each order and start adding two years for each date value.

02:32.220 --> 02:33.740
Now let's check another example.

02:33.740 --> 02:35.820
Here we are saying date add month.

02:35.820 --> 02:38.300
So here we want to manipulate the month parts.

02:38.300 --> 02:40.540
But here we are saying minus four.

02:40.620 --> 02:46.580
That means we want to go and subtract four months from each value in the order date.

02:46.580 --> 02:51.020
So as you can see the value of the interval whether it's positive or negative, we are controlling here

02:51.020 --> 02:54.100
the function whether it is subtraction or addition.

02:54.100 --> 02:58.660
So let's have a few examples about the date add using our field order dates.

02:58.660 --> 03:01.860
So for example let's go and add two years for each date.

03:02.100 --> 03:04.500
So we can do it like this date adds.

03:04.500 --> 03:05.700
So we are adding years.

03:05.700 --> 03:10.060
That's why we're going to go with the part here and how many years we are adding we are adding two years.

03:10.060 --> 03:12.620
So this is our interval and our field.

03:12.820 --> 03:14.700
Our value is the order date.

03:14.700 --> 03:17.060
So now in the output as you can see we got a date.

03:17.060 --> 03:20.940
But this date is always two years higher than the order dates.

03:20.940 --> 03:23.860
So everywhere you have see 2027.

03:23.860 --> 03:27.420
Now let's go and add maybe three months for each date.

03:27.460 --> 03:30.620
Just going to go and copy it and say a month.

03:30.620 --> 03:36.930
Let's change the interval to Three and we're going to call it three months later.

03:36.930 --> 03:39.410
So now if you check the output over here, we have a new date.

03:39.410 --> 03:44.370
But now the difference between it and the order date we have here always three months more than the

03:44.370 --> 03:45.170
order dates.

03:45.170 --> 03:47.530
So for example here we have January.

03:47.530 --> 03:49.890
But in the new one we have April.

03:49.890 --> 03:52.170
And for the next one we have February.

03:52.290 --> 03:53.890
And in the new field we have my.

03:53.930 --> 03:56.490
So as you can see we are adding months over here.

03:56.490 --> 04:00.570
So as you can see we are adding months to our original field order dates.

04:00.610 --> 04:03.890
Now let's say that I would like to go and subtract ten days.

04:03.890 --> 04:05.770
So let's go and do the same.

04:05.770 --> 04:07.690
So we're going to have the date add.

04:07.730 --> 04:11.930
Since we are talking about the days, it's going to be the day we can subtract ten days.

04:11.930 --> 04:14.690
So minus ten for the order date.

04:14.690 --> 04:20.810
So let's call it ten days before let's go and execute it.

04:20.810 --> 04:22.490
Now we got as well a new date.

04:22.490 --> 04:27.010
And this date has always ten days before the order date.

04:27.010 --> 04:31.250
So for example let's take the order number seven and the order date we have 15.

04:31.290 --> 04:33.090
But in the new column we have five.

04:33.490 --> 04:37.730
So we have subtracted ten days from the original field order dates.

04:37.730 --> 04:43.770
So as you can see it's very simple to add or subtract days year months using the date add.
